scripts/wechat_key_verify.py adapts the first-page HMAC and passphrase
derivation algorithm. It adds bounded read-only file access, candidate-file
permission checks, aggregate-only output, and fail-closed validation.
Upstream memory scanning, debugger capture, caching, and decryption are not
included or executed by that verification tool.

scripts/wechat_lldb_capture.py independently implements an experimental
hardware breakpoint at the upstream CCKeyDerivationPBKDF capture point.
It restricts the target, parameters and account salts, uses private output,
and explicitly detaches without the upstream global debugger cleanup.

The packaged equivalents live in resources/macos/login-capture/.
electron/services/wechatLoginCaptureService.ts also adapts the SQLCipher 4
first-page HMAC algorithm for in-process account verification.

The same algorithm is used by electron/services/wechatLoginCaptureService.ts.
The canonical Python verifier and a separately implemented supervised LLDB
capture live in resources/macos/login-capture; scripts provide compatibility
entry points. The capture point and CommonCrypto argument mapping follow the
upstream revision above. Its global debugger termination and key cache logic
are not used.
